  "description": {
    "text": "The deck that won the Senior Division of the 2017 World Championships, a Water deck built on Alolan Ninetales-GX, with Aqua Patch to power it up and Rough Seas to heal the team. Ice Blade can hit the Bench, Blizzard Edge hits hard, and Ice Path-GX moves all of Alolan Ninetales-GX's damage counters to the opponent's Active Pokémon. The 2017 World Championships were held at the Anaheim Convention Center in Anaheim, California, from 18 to 20 August 2017.\n\nPokémon sold it as a 2017 World Championships deck: a 60-card copy of the deck with a booklet, a deck box and a pin. Its cards have a limited-edition back, a silver border and the player's signature on the picture, and are not legal in tournaments."
  },
  "tell": {
    "text": "A gray border, and a player's signature on the picture"
  },
